      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a lot to take in. so if the nakba is such a central part of the historical reality, how do historians view the israeli side's justifications for all that? like, was there a valid counter-argument to the displacement, or is it just seen as an intentional strategy by the militias?",
      "source": "evaluator"
